{"actor":"agent:cairn-tab-bar","data":{"complexity":"low","description":"scripts/smoke-test-ci.sh sends the v1 socket command 'send time\\n' about 2.5s after launch with a 5s recv timeout. On the macOS virtual-display runner the initial terminal can take up to 3.0s to attach ('Welcome quad: initial terminal not ready after 3.0s'), and the send handler waits up to 2.0s for a surface, so the test has ~zero margin. Seen once on #463 (run 36786196112 attempt 1); attempt 2 on the same head passed, and local repro under load answered in 0.03s. Fix: wait for a ready, focused terminal (poll a readiness command) before sending, or retry the send once; don't touch app code.","priority":"low","short_id":"C11-247","status":"backlog","tags":["ci","flake"],"title":"Smoke test: 'send time' can time out on a slow CI launch","type":"bug"},"id":"ev_01M3T9RNQWEBB2JV4AZ51GDM9F","origin":{"op":"task.create","op_id":"op_01M3T9RNQE17NP2G5H0BD9077D","reported":{"branch":"main","client_version":"0.2.1","host":"Hyperion","os_user":"atin","worktree":"/Users/atin/Projects/Stage11/code/c11"}},"schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01M3T9RNQG4MTPSCNAT0VZPRCM","ts":"2026-09-30T23:18:01Z","type":"task_created"}
